epos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.6.3.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.3.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.7.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Apple M1 - Apple M1 (8 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe macOS VoiceOver screenreader _recognizes_ Godot buttons, and offers to click them, but they don't respond. VO makes a sound indicating that it thinks it has clicked the button. The button does respond to space or to a mouse click, so it's not broken.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUsing the minimal reproduction project below, make and run a Mac build. Use VoiceOver to navigate to a button. (The navigation controls don't obey the structure within Godot, but that's a separate issue). Try using the VO command (ctrl-option-space) to click the button. The text on the button *should* change (and it does if you just hit space or click on the button), but it doesn't.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nUse commit f5e074 from this repository:\n\nhttps://github.com/PeterDrake/screenreader","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120324/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120324/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}